<title>USA: U.S. to provide $200 mln insurance for Oman LNG.</title>
<headline>U.S. to provide $200 mln insurance for Oman LNG.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Overseas Private Investment Corp said Wednesday it would provide $200 million in political risk insurance to Chase Manhattan Bank for loans to Oman's liquefied natural gas project.</p>
<p>OPIC President Ruth Harkin announced the move in Cairo, OPIC said in a statement released here. Harkin said it &quot;reaffirms the Clinton Administration's and OPIC's long-term commitment to economic development in this important region.&quot;</p>
<p>Exports from the $6 billion LNG joint venture project are set to begin in 2000.</p>
</text>
